'''Tarfful''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Wookiee]] [[chief]]tain and [[general]] who helped defend his native [[planet]] [[Kashyyyk]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. During the war, he led a band of Wookiees to answer a distress signal made by [[Chewbacca]], who was imprisoned on the [[Trandoshan]] hunting grounds of [[Wasskah]]. Tarfful later participated in the [[Battle of Kashyyyk]] alongside Chewbacca and [[Jedi Master]] [[Yoda]]. In the wake of [[Order 66]] and the rise of the [[Galactic Empire]], Tarfful helped facilitate Yoda's escape and continued fighting against the tyranny of the Empire in the following years.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Good-bye, Tarfful. Good-bye, Chewbacca. Miss you I will.|Yoda, shortly before his departure from Kashyyyk|audio=Yoda-MissYouIWill.flac|<ref name="Episode III" />}}
At some point prior to the [[Great Jedi Purge]], Tarfful met and befriended [[Jedi Master]] [[Eno Cordova]], and helped him navigate [[Kashyyyk]] to learn about [[Zeffonian]] culture.<ref name="Fallen Order" />

[[File:Ramy_thrown-WH.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Tarfful throwing a [[Ramy|Trandoshan]] off of the [[Ubrikkian Floating Fortress|floating fortress]].]]
A male [[Wookiee]] native to his [[species]]'s [[homeworld]] of Kashyyyk, Tarfful served as the [[chief]]tain of the coastal [[city]] [[Kachirho]] at the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> He also held the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[general]] among his people.<ref name="SWETarfful" />

One [[standard year]] into the war, one of Tarfful's fellow Wookiees, [[Chewbacca]], was captured by [[Trandoshan]]s and taken to [[Wasskah]] to be [[Hunting|hunted]] for sport. There, Chewbacca managed to build a device which sent a [[distress signal]] to Kashyyyk. Upon hearing of his friend's situation, Tarfful hired the [[bounty hunter]]s [[Sugi (bounty hunter)|Sugi]] and [[Seripas]] to [[transport]] him and a group of his most trusted [[Soldier|warriors]] to Wasskah. Once there, the chieftain and his men made [[Battle on Wasskah|quick work]] of the Trandoshan hunters, overpowering them and rescuing Chewbacca, as well as [[Jedi]] [[youngling]]s [[Ahsoka Tano]], [[Jinx]], and [[O-Mer]].<ref name="Wookiee Hunt">{{TCW|Wookiee Hunt}}</ref>

[[File:Tarfful-TSWB.png|thumb|right|220px|Tarfful defended his world from Separatist invasion.]]
At one point, Tarfful was captured by Trandoshan slavers who had made a deal with [[Count]] [[Dooku]],<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> but he was [[Rescue of Tarfful|rescued]]<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> by a squad of [[clone commando]]s soon after.<ref name="CVD" /> Tarfful took part in the [[Battle of Kashyyyk]] alongside Chewbacca and [[Jedi General]]s [[Yoda]], [[Luminara Unduli]] and [[Quinlan Vos]].<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> Aided by the [[Grand Army of the Republic]], he led the [[Kachirho Wookiee Militia]] against the invading [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[droid]] [[Confederacy military|forces]]. Following the implementation of [[Order 66]], Tarfful and Chewbacca helped Yoda elude the [[clone trooper]]s and escape from the [[planet]] in a [[Wookiee escape pod]].<ref name="Episode III" />

In the wake of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s rise, Tarfful's anti-Imperial stance made him a wanted criminal, forcing him to take shelter in the [[Shadowlands]].<ref name="TSWB">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref>

In [[14 BBY]], [[Saw Gerrera]]'s rebel cell, the [[Partisans]], agreed to help [[Cal Kestis]] and the crew of the ''[[Stinger Mantis]]'' track down Tarfful, as the Wookiee chieftain was aware of information that could aid the Jedi Padawan in locating a [[Jedi holocron]] containing a list of names of several [[Force-sensitive]] children. After locating Tarfful in the [[Shadowlands]], the majority of the Partisans evacuated Kashyyyk, whilst Wookiee Commander [[Choyyssyk]] and Partisan [[Mari Kosan]] remained with Tarfful. Tarfful later provided the information Kestis was seeking upon the Padawan's return to Kashyyyk.<ref name="Fallen Order" />

[[Standard decade|Decade]]s later, a picture of Tarfful was in the ''[[Galactic Explorer's Guide]]'', a survival guide written by [[Hondo Ohnaka]] and [[DK-RA-43]].<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref>

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Fortitude-CM.png|thumb|left|250px|Tarfful was a fierce warrior.]]
Tarfful was a massive Wookiee who stood at 2.32 [[meter]]s (7 [[Foot|feet]], 7 inches),<ref name="Join the Battle" /> was covered with [[Color|dark brown]] fur, had blue [[eye]]s,<ref name="Episode III" /> and wore [[armor]] around his shoulders and chest. He demonstrated great loyalty and trust amongst his warriors and allies, traits that were held in high honor in Wookiee culture.<ref name="Wookiees">{{SWE|groups|wookiees|Wookiees}}</ref>

He worked closely with Chewbacca during the Clone Wars and was considered a dear friend by [[Jedi Master]] Yoda.<ref name="SWETarfful" /> Although an ally of the Republic, Tarfful was primarily focused on the governing of Kashyyyk.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> With the dawn of the Galactic Empire, Tarfful would fight against the regime and become a symbol of Wookiee resistance.<ref name="Fallen Order" />

==Skills and abilities==
Tarfful was a powerful Wookiee chieftain and general, known for his leadership and military tactics. He was skilled in both armed and unarmed combat.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> Tarfful fought with a [[Kashyyyk long-gun]]<ref name="Episode III" /> and could also overwhelm opponents such as Trandoshans in hand-to-hand combat.<ref name="Wookiee Hunt" /> 

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Join Tarfful and Cradossk to lead your forces into battle!|"Fierce Enemies" caption for ''Star Wars: Galactic Defense''|<ref name="Galactic Defense">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Defense]]''</ref>}}
Tarfful was played by [[Michael Kingma]] in [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Revenge of the Sith'']]. He originally appeared in the [[2005]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] video game ''[[Star Wars: Republic Commando]]''.

According to the ''Revenge of the Sith'' DVD text commentary, during Yoda's "goodbye" scene to Chewbacca and Tarfful in the film, Tarfful's roar is actually [[Attichitcuk/Legends|Itchy's]] roar from ''[[The Star Wars Holiday Special]]''.

In the [[2014]] mobile game ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Defense]]'', Tarfful can be seen yelling "hnn-rowr yrroonn nng rarr," a quote which first appeared in the [[Canon|Legends]] comic ''[[Star Wars: Empire's End]]'' and meant "long live the [[New Republic]]," when translated from [[Shyriiwook]].

Tarfful was introduced as a playable character of the same name in the 2015 mobile game ''Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes'' in 2023, which features characters from both the canon and Legends continuities.<ref name="GoH">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]''</ref>

